**Findings**
1. High: the live boundary was not preserving the prior snapshot, so “Latest change” and the polite live-region copy were derived from current state instead of real refresh deltas. Fixed in [DashboardLiveScreen.tsx](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/components/DashboardLiveScreen.tsx), [tanstack-react-query.tsx](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/lib/vendor/tanstack-react-query.tsx), and [dashboard-presenter.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/presenters/dashboard-presenter.js).
2. High: after the first refresh, the announcement path could keep resurfacing the same non-live condition instead of only newly changed meaning. Fixed by feeding real previous/current snapshot pairs into the presenter in [DashboardLiveScreen.tsx](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/components/DashboardLiveScreen.tsx) and tightening delta logic in [dashboard-presenter.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/presenters/dashboard-presenter.js).
3. Medium: nearby-mode change summaries only described worsening states and omitted calm recovery wording, which weakened reduced-motion comprehension. Fixed in [dashboard-presenter.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/presenters/dashboard-presenter.js) with regression coverage in [dashboard.presenter.test.mjs](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/tests/unit/dashboard.presenter.test.mjs).

No remaining high or medium findings in the reviewed story scope. I also updated the story record to `done` in [2-5-maintain-stable-live-reading-during-updates-and-motion-changes.md](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/sprint-artifacts/2-5-maintain-stable-live-reading-during-updates-and-motion-changes.md) and synced sprint tracking in [sprint-status.yaml](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/sprint-artifacts/sprint-status.yaml).

Verification passed: `npm run test:unit -- tests/unit/dashboard.presenter.test.mjs tests/unit/dashboard.live-path.test.mjs`, `node --test tests/smoke/startup-smoke.test.mjs`, and `npm run validate`. I ignored [logs/ralph-20260319-072518.log](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/logs/ralph-20260319-072518.log) during review because the workflow excludes non-application source files.
