/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/ux-design-specification.md:44:The second challenge is preserving composure while presenting live, multi-source information. Albemarle Pulse has to combine weather, mobility status, trend, and trust cues into one calm surface without feeling like a dashboard, route planner, or live-ops monitor. Too much detail and too much switching are already the problem, so the UX must make synthesis easier rather than expose more operational complexity.
/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/ux-design-specification.md:74:Mouse and keyboard interaction should exist only for setup, maintenance, and recovery. This keeps the public-facing experience disciplined and protects the product's identity as a shared foyer instrument rather than a kiosk or personal utility app.
/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/ux-design-specification.md:166:Flighty is a strong reference for honesty under changing conditions and for the way it turns volatile operational information into user confidence rather than noise. Its value is not just status visibility, but status prioritization: it makes clear what changed, what matters, and what is uncertain. For Albemarle Pulse, this is directly relevant to trend visibility, freshness handling, disruption honesty, and the need to preserve trust even when conditions deteriorate or one source weakens.
/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/ux-design-specification.md:168:**TfL wayfinding and line-status signage**
/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/ux-design-specification.md:169:TfL's public wayfinding and status signage is the most relevant reference for shared public readability. It is built for mixed audiences in motion, designed to be understood quickly at a distance, and trusted because it feels familiar, direct, and physically usable in public space. This makes it the strongest model for Albemarle Pulse's public-display character, especially its need for shared orientation, distance legibility, and calm factual clarity without app-like interaction.
/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/ux-design-specification.md:180:Borrow the TfL signage pattern of designing for fast reading by mixed audiences in physical motion. In Albemarle Pulse, this supports high-distance legibility, shared group readability, familiar status grammar, and a non-interactive main screen.
/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/ux-design-specification.md:202:- Adopt Flighty's status honesty and prioritization because they support trustworthy live conditions, selective freshness, and clear disruption handling.
/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/ux-design-specification.md:232:- restrained, display-specific status and motion language
/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/ux-design-specification.md:244:- status tokens for calm, trustworthy condition signaling
/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/ux-design-specification.md:255:Customization should be led by design tokens first, components second. The foundational layer should define the product's visual and behavioral grammar through custom tokens for type scale, spacing, color, contrast, status states, motion timing, and surface treatment.
/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/ux-design-specification.md:283:Current tools feel magical when one of them provides a fast trustworthy status or a familiar map immediately. They feel terrible when they require switching, destination entry, too much private detail, unclear freshness, conflicting information, or too much effort at exactly the wrong moment.
